      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOLD CHALICE (3) looks the one to beat off a good debut at Geelong back in June, in the market there and showing pace, only beaten a nose in third. Set a good bar for the others to reach there and with natural improvement should go close. COME TOGETHER (1) might be the main danger on debut. He's a gelding by Maurice for the Price & Kent Jnr yard who has won a few jumpouts leading in and looks ready to go, respect. HYDRO RUSH (4) is a Headwater colt on debut for the Pace yard who has won a trial and gets Blake Shinn on, watch betting. DESERT OAK (2) has jumped out quite well and can run a good race.",
